$DIR/main.p:18:9: append is not permitted in Plutonium (a slice cannot grow; use pluto/vec)
    Plutonium has no append. In Go, append grows a slice by allocating a larger
    array behind the program's back, and the garbage collector frees the old
    one. A Plutonium slice is a view of an array that something else owns, so it
    cannot grow.
    Use a vec.Vec from pluto/vec, which owns its array and grows it from an
    allocator. To fill a slice's spare capacity without growing it, slice it
    longer and assign, or use copy.
    Plutonium has no garbage collector and never allocates memory unless the
    program asks for it in the code, so that every cost is visible and the same
    code can run inside a kernel.
    To fill buf without allocating, use a vec.Fixed over it, which keeps what
    fits:
        import "pluto/vec"

        b := vec.NewFixed(buf[:])
        b.Append('a', 'b')
        // b.Slice() holds the elements; b.Truncated() reports what did not fit
    (see "Built-ins Plutonium does not have" in the Plutonium spec, section
    13.1)
    (run "pluto explain E2013" for a longer explanation)

